From 1f2995f1a446c59c0b3db7c0770860b40e659bb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 11:47:58 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/39] v4.7-gpu: fix SMT interactive placement to respect task
 CPU affinity

The SMT interactive placement hook could move a waking task to the
primary thread of its core even when that CPU is outside the task's
allowed mask (cpuset or sched_setaffinity restriction).  The pre-existing
select_idle_sibling() path guarantees new_cpu is in p->cpus_ptr, but the
sibling core is not checked.

Gate the move on cpumask_test_cpu() so the wakeup target always honors
the task's affinity, avoiding placement on a disallowed CPU and the
migration thrash that follows.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
---
 kernel/sched/fair.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
index 6ad682033..9691b5ed2 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -9840,7 +9840,13 @@ select_task_rq_fair(struct task_struct *p, int prev_cpu, int wake_flags)
 			int primary = cpumask_first(
 				topology_sibling_cpumask(new_cpu));
 
+			/*
+			 * The primary thread must be allowed for this task:
+			 * select_idle_sibling() guarantees new_cpu is in
+			 * p->cpus_ptr, but the sibling core may not be.
+			 */
 			if (primary != new_cpu &&
+			    cpumask_test_cpu(primary, p->cpus_ptr) &&
 			    available_idle_cpu(primary)) {
 				new_cpu = primary;
 				atomic_inc(this_cpu_ptr(&infinity_smt_interactive_count));
