From 0026fc298025095a86a06605f09fcfc3e00d0253 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 14:31:04 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/39] v4.7-gpu: fix infinity_stats sysctl read returning
 EFAULT

The infinity_stats handler copied its formatted table to userspace with
simple_read_from_buffer(), but since the sysctl core refactor the buffer
handed to proc handlers is kernel-allocated and the core copies it to
userspace itself.  copy_to_user() on that kernel address fails access_ok,
so every read returned -EFAULT ("Bad address").

Route the output through proc_dostring() on a const ctl_table instead,
which writes into the kernel buffer with memcpy and preserves partial-
read, EOF and trailing-newline behavior.  Read-only semantics are
unchanged.

Restore the description-column separator to 32 characters to match the
%-30s rows again; the 27-character separator no longer lined up with
the row borders once the descriptions grew.  The separator is declared
without const to stay within checkpatch's 100-column limit.

Scale the stats table to any counter magnitude: format every count,
including the accounting-confidence audit line, with K/M/B/T/Qa/Qi
suffixes (two decimals, floor-truncated) so the output is bounded to 8
characters and the columns never shift, and widen the per-CPU counters
from atomic_t to atomic64_t so the totals stay exact instead of
wrapping at 2^31 per CPU under sustained load.  Percentage and average
math uses mul_u64_u32_div() so it cannot overflow for any u64 value.

Fix the stray double parenthesis in the per-CPU counter exports that
prevented the 6.18 and Fedora 7.0 targets from compiling, and cast the
version string at its sysctl table entry so the build no longer warns
about discarding the const qualifier.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
