From e15b43da27013293dc9887a39db4ff85cc1ff9bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 15:04:55 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 18/39] v4.8-gpu: add hysteresis and rate limit to the RT
 safety valve

Dual threshold (engage 95%, re-arm 85%) removes boundary oscillation;
the requeue-time decay of rt_ema is required, because rt_ema climbs
only on consume and decays only on wakeup, so without it the release
threshold is unreachable for a continuously running rogue.  The decay
quantum (100 ms) leaves ~57% of the EMA, dropping a 95% burner below
the re-arm point in one requeue.  The jiffies-based window is
global-safe under NO_HZ_FULL tick offload and gates both requeue and
resched.  Documented interaction: the decayed rt_ema also widens the
RR timeslice (infinity_rr_timeslice reads rt_ema) during the
valve-release phase -- bounded by the same EMA math and accepted.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
