From 5a5fbf7398bb6bb37684d1eda3c5d13c33e9f08e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 15:05:10 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/39] v4.8-gpu: gate GPU coupling on the fair scheduler class

The DRM scheduler's CPU<->GPU coupling reads the owning task's CPU-side
interactivity signals (futex_waiting, ema == 0) and the passover loop
accumulates gpu_passovers for every entity further right in the vtime
rbtree.  Because infinity_pid is the process group leader (captured via
get_task_pid(current->group_leader) at drm_sched_entity_init), both
paths now gate on the leader's sched_class via the new exported helper
infinity_is_interactive_candidate(): fair-class, non-idle-policy only.

Non-CFS leaders (sched_ext, RT, DL) no longer have their untouched
ema == 0 misread as interactive, and no longer accumulate gpu_passovers.
SCHED_IDLE-policy leaders are excluded as well -- the mirror of the
calc_weight bypass.  The coupling counters are reused unchanged (they
only fire when the boost is applied); no new counters.

Conservative default for scx GPU workloads: they lose the interactive
GPU boost until validated (documented policy).  The helper is exported
with EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL as a scheduler-internal interface.

7.2-series placement: the upstreamed FAIR DRM scheduler layout moves
this coupling out of sched_main.c into sched_rq.c.  The CPU->GPU reads
are gated in drm_sched_entity_update_vruntime() and the gpu_passovers
accumulation loop in drm_sched_select_entity() (both in sched_rq.c);
the 7.1 sched_main.c hunks do not apply (drm_sched_entity_calc_vtime
and drm_sched_rq_select_entity_infinity are absent in the 7.2 tree).
The prototype is added to include/drm/gpu_scheduler.h and the helper
to kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c, ported as-is from the 7.1 series.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
