From 97a244769818e714c7d8cd0d218a43405401edc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 18:29:15 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 31/39] v4.8-gpu: pair lockless infinity_ctx access with
 READ_ONCE/WRITE_ONCE

The audit flagged the lockless cross-CPU accesses to struct infinity_ctx
as formal data races (KCSAN-class; benign on 64-bit but torn reads are
possible on 32-bit).  Every reader now uses READ_ONCE and every writer
WRITE_ONCE across ema, rt_ema, futex_waiting, ipc_waiting,
ipc_last_boost, rt_valve_armed, rt_valve_last_jiffies, last_sleep_ns,
group_ema and group_ema_sleep_start.  wait_woken() additionally stores
ipc_waiting BEFORE the task state store, so the waker's try_to_wake_up --
which pairs with the state store -- reliably observes the flag before the
task can be scheduled; the unconditional set/clear is harmless on the
WQ_FLAG_WOKEN fast path because the enqueue that consumes the flag
already happened before WOKEN was set, and the flag is cleared again
before the task can run further.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
---
 kernel/futex/waitwake.c       |  4 +--
 kernel/sched/fair.c           | 41 ++++++++++++++++--------------
 kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c | 48 +++++++++++++++++++----------------
 kernel/sched/rt.c             | 14 +++++-----
 kernel/sched/wait.c           | 15 +++++++----
 5 files changed, 67 insertions(+), 55 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/futex/waitwake.c b/kernel/futex/waitwake.c
index ea2dc0839..193b06c5c 100644
--- a/kernel/futex/waitwake.c
+++ b/kernel/futex/waitwake.c
@@ -385,9 +385,9 @@ void futex_do_wait(struct futex_q *q, struct hrtimer_sleeper *timeout)
