clamp_smt_divisor() clamped out-of-range writes after the fact, leaving a
window where an out-of-range value was briefly visible to scheduler
ticks between the proc store and the clamp.  extra1/extra2 on the sysctl
table entry let the proc layer validate atomically inside the write, so
out-of-range writes are now rejected instead of silently clamped; the
handler only reports changes.

